OL,3,GNEWSAResident fined #600 after firm
OL,4,Afly-tipped rubbish
OL,5,
OL,6,FA household in Leicestershire has been
OL,7,Ffined #600 after a waste disposal firm
OL,8,Fthat was hired to clear rubbish from
OL,9,Fthe property fly-tipped the waste.
OL,11,FCharnwood Borough Council said the
OL,12,Fresident paid #150 for the service but
OL,13,Ffailed to check whether the operator
OL,14,Fwas a legitimate, registered waste
OL,15,Fcarrier.
OL,17,FThe rubbish, which included a
OL,18,Ftelevision, laptop, metal wiring and a
OL,19,Frug, was later found dumped in
OL,20,FRidgemere Lane on the outskirts of
OL,21,FQueniborough.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
